#: dist/js/synonyms-script.js:1
msgid "<p><strong>Hyponyms</strong> are terms with a more specific meaning than another more generic terms, called a <strong>hypernym</strong>. For example, <em>aqua</em>, <em>azure</em>, and <em>cerulean</em> are all hyponyms of <em>blue</em>, their hypernym.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/synonyms/components/groups/hyponyms.js:32
#: dist/js/synonyms-script.js:1
msgid "<p>Use hyponyms when you want search queries for a parent term to return results relevant to itself or any of its child terms, but search queries for a child term to only return results that are relevant to that term. For example, when a search for \"blue\" should return anything blue, whether it be aqua, azure, or cerulean, but a search for \"cerulean\" should return only items that are specifically cerulean blue.</p>"
msgstr ""

